Three statements each missing a required piece: an empty right-hand side
(`nTotal := ;`, the `;` is unexpected), an empty :IF condition, and the
non-existent `**=` compound assignment (issue #260). One unexpected_token
per statement, no cascade; the :IF block still pairs
(diag.unexpected_token).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE BrokenMath;
	:DECLARE nTotal, nBase;
	nBase := 2;
	nTotal := ;
	:IF;
		nTotal := 1;
	:ENDIF;
	nBase **= 3;
	:RETURN nTotal;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE BrokenMath;
	:DECLARE nTotal, nBase;
	nBase := 2;
	nTotal :=;
	:IF;
		nTotal := 1;
	:ENDIF;
	nBase ** = 3;
	:RETURN nTotal;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
